abstract: >-
  Artifact backing the paper "The Hypothesis Graph: Semantic Memory Written by
  Methodeutics". A mechanism case study on whether an LLM generalizes a bug fix
  to a represented predicate or merely tabulates the reported case. On a Verus
  verifier soundness bug (#2219, post-cutoff) whose correct fix is an XOR-shaped
  predicate, it isolates where prompt-encoded methods, an execution-gated
  evaluation tool, and cross-model capability each do or do not lift the fix, and
  shows that enumeration is inducible by the model while the calibration oracle
  (external ground truth) is not. Includes the forced-fresh identity-verified
  grading harness, the case arms (codex, Fable, Sonnet 4.6, Composer 2.5), the
  out-of-grammar held-outs, the full reasoning trail, and reproduction
  instructions. An existence proof of a mechanism, not a resolve-rate claim.
